NOTE[en]="Estimated figures based on available information from two web scrapers, http://tomslee.net/ and http://airdna.co, enriched with data from Statistics Iceland. It is expected that in 2016, approximately 3600 rooms / apartments were rented regularly through"
" Airbnb's website, including around 2000 in the capital area. It is clear that the availability of accommodation is not stable over the year and it is difficult to estimate the exact availability and utilization of accommodation space. According to Airdn"
"a.co data, most of the properties are leased out 1-3 months (38%) per year, but the fewest (15%) are leased out 10-12 months a year.";
